pipeline: split blocks end where their settings change, as InDesign does

Consecutive SplitColumns paragraphs were merged into one block on the
first paragraph's count and gutters. Measured with the new paged-gen
fixture split-boundaries (24 cases, InDesign 2025 DOM + PDF):
- a new block starts where SpanSplitColumnCount, the inside gutter or the
  outside gutter changes; min-space-only differences and spelled-out
  defaults stay one block; the next block starts directly below the
  deepest sub-column of the last, balanced on its own.
- spacing at every split-block boundary = max(SpaceAfter + SpaceBefore,
  ending block's SpanColumnMinSpaceAfter, starting block's
  SpanColumnMinSpaceBefore).
- text balanced above a span that holds a split block is set at the least
  column height at which it all fits, the split filling its sub-columns
  to that height.
